# Creating a New PIE Element

*This tutorial will guide you through designing and building a custom PIE element from scratch.*

## Overview

In this tutorial, you'll learn:

- How to design a new question type
- Which PIE interfaces to implement
- How to package your element for distribution
- How to set up a new project in pie-elements (or as a standalone project)

## Coming Soon

This comprehensive tutorial is currently being developed and will cover:

### 1. Planning Your Element

- Identifying the assessment need
- Sketching the student interaction
- Defining the data model
- Planning the scoring logic

### 2. Understanding the PIE Element Interface

- Required properties: `configuration` and `model`
- Web Component lifecycle
- Event handling
- State management

### 3. Project Structure

```
my-element/
├── controller/           # Server-side logic
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── index.js     # model() and outcome()
│   │   └── schema.json  # Configuration schema
│   └── package.json
├── src/                 # Client-side element
│   ├── index.js         # Web Component
│   └── styles.css
├── configure/           # Authoring interface (optional)
│   └── src/
│       └── index.js
└── package.json
```

### 4. Setting Up in pie-elements

- Cloning vs. creating new
- Monorepo structure
- Shared dependencies
- Build configuration

### 5. Development Workflow

- Local development setup
- Testing your element
- Debugging tools
- Integration testing

### 6. Packaging & Distribution

- NPM package configuration
- Versioning strategy
- Documentation requirements
- Publishing to npm

